// case: assignment-type-mismatch
// what: a `var` declared int is given a string. The target is never checked,
//      so the builder keeps `x` typed int while the value is a string; the
//      emitted C calls `print("%s", x)` with an integer and the program dies
//      with an access violation, printing nothing.
// known-defect: F-0025
// no-diagnostic:
fn main() -> int {
    var x: int = 1
    x = "s"
    print(x)
    return 0
}
